<title>INDIA: India Hoechst 96/97 1st half net up 30 pct.</title>
<headline>India Hoechst 96/97 1st half net up 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		168.30 vs   129.20</p>
<p>    Net sales	     2,096.30 vs 1,696.80</p>
<p>    Other income	     82.20 vs    73.50</p>
<p>    Total expenditure   1,811.70 vs 1,473.70</p>
<p>    Interest costs	   62.70 vs    44.40</p>
<p>    Gross Profit	    304.10 vs   252.20</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     53.80 vs    48.00</p>
<p>    Tax			  82.00 vs    75.00</p>
<p>Note:Hoechst Marion Roussel Ltd is the Indian affiliate of the German pharmaceutical multinational.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom -91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
